# Pinned upstream fork + commit SHA for the source-build fallback.
# Build.rakumod fetches this exact commit via `git init` + fetch-by-SHA
# so a moving branch can never silently change what we build.
#
# When bumping:
#   1. Push the new commit to the URL below.
#   2. Update the sha= line to the new HEAD.
#   3. Sync vendor/notcurses to match (CI prebuilt lanes still read
#      from vendor; collapse onto the fetch once CI is migrated).
#   4. Bump BINARY_TAG so consumers re-pull the prebuilt that
#      embeds the new patch.
#
# Lines starting with `#` and blank lines are ignored. Keys are
# case-sensitive; `url=` and `sha=` are required.
url=https://github.com/m-doughty/notcurses.git
